---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How Ethotechnics Works — Governance for Reversible AI"
  description="See how Ethotechnics turns governance principles into operational defaults that cap burden, assign accountable owners, and keep high-stakes decisions reversible."
  structuredDataType="webpage"
>
  <section class="stack-lg institute-screen">
    <h1>How Ethotechnics works</h1>
    <p>
      Ethotechnics governs system failure, not intent.<br /><br />
      It provides operational artifacts that make decisions reversible, assign ownership
      under pressure, and cap the burden placed on affected users.<br /><br />
      If you need adoptable defaults, use the Institute. If you need installation,
      rehearsal, or binding enforcement, use the Studio.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="/#failure-intake">Start with a failure</a>
      <a class="button" href="/artifacts">Browse artifacts</a>
      <a class="button ghost" href="/standards">Review standards</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
